Four languages over the same C ABI archives, one of the three consumption
[surfaces]($link.page('surfaces')). Each binding mirrors the archive set: a core
over `libpancake_ocapn` / `libpancake_driver`, plus per-transport modules loaded
à la carte. Capability ideas: [Concepts]($link.page('concepts')).

[All four bindings wrap the same C ABI. The shared surface is what lets an app read the same way in every language.]($image.siteAsset('diagram-bindings.svg'))

## One surface, four idioms

Hold a `Session` and the verbs in the
[bindings contract](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/bindings/README.md).
A `Host` is the multi-session product behind introductions
([modules]($link.page('modules'))). A `Ref` is a capability in hand; pass it as
an argument and authority moves.

| Binding | Entry point | Async idiom | Actor idiom |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| [Rust]($link.page('bindings/rust')) | `connect`, `Session`, typed enums | tokio (opt-in `async`) | `spawn` over closures |
| [TypeScript]($link.page('bindings/ts')) | `connect`, `Session` class | native promises | `spawn` over callbacks |
| [Python]($link.page('bindings/python')) | `connect`, `Session`, native values | `asyncio` | `spawn` over callables |
| [Racket]($link.page('bindings/racket')) | `connect`, `session`, event structs | green threads + ports | Goblins-faithful |

`connect(locator)` returns an established session (handshake complete). All four
ride the shared byte-fed host.

## Levels

Stay at the level you need: sync verbs, the language's own async sockets, or the
Goblins-shaped actor top. Vat / `$` / `<-`: [modules]($link.page('modules')).

## Archives and encryption

No prebuilt archives yet. Run `zig build` in a checkout, then point
`PANCAKE_LIB_DIR` or use `zig-out/lib`. Encrypted transport is optional
[iroh]($link.page('transports/iroh')).

```sh
zig build bindings        # rust + deno + bun + python + racket smokes
zig build rust-dogfood    # just Rust
```

Needs `cargo`, `deno`, `bun`, `python3`, and `racket` on PATH (or the
[devcontainer](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/.devcontainer/)).
